<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Subutai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Subutai was one of the leading generals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> and his successor Ögedei. He led campaigns across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> profile treats him as one of the most successful military commanders in history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/subutai.jpg" alt="Subutai" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: неизвестен/unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Subudei.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
